{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Moses caused Israel to journey.</b> Rashi explained: 'וַיַּסַּע' — he moved them against their will, for they did not want to depart from the spoil of the sea. And Moses feared lest the abundance of wealth bring them to sin, and the episode of the calf proves it, for the abundance of gold that was showered upon them was the cause of its making. Therefore he moved them against their will. And Moses further reckoned that the abundance of wealth would be a cause that they would not be worthy to receive the Torah, for Torah and wealth flee from one another, and they are as rivals to one another, as it is written (Psalms 119:71), ״טוֹב לִי כִי עֻנֵּיתִי לְמַעַן אֶלְמַד חֻקֶּיךָ״. Therefore he moved them against their will." "<b>And they went three days in the wilderness and found no water.</b> Measure for measure: because they occupied themselves with the spoil of the sea more than was proper, and from then on they were unworthy to receive the Torah, which is likened to water, therefore they were punished in that they found no water. And this is the view of our Rabbis of blessed memory in tractate Bava Kamma (82b): ״דּוֹרְשֵׁי רְשׁוּמוֹת אָמְרוּ שֶׁהָלְכוּ שְׁלֹשֶׁת יָמִים בַּמִּדְבָּר בְּלֹא תּוֹרָה שֶׁנִּמְשְׁלָה לַמַּיִם״, etc. And without a doubt they did not intend to say that this lack of water was itself the Torah, for if so, what would they do with the casting of the wood into the water? Rather, they meant to say that because through being occupied with the spoil and not hurrying to go to the wilderness, the place of receiving the Torah, therefore they were punished that they did not find water simpliciter. For the Holy One, blessed be He, had already said to them, ״תַּעַבְדוּן אֶת הָאֱלֹהִים עַל הָהָר הַזֶּה״ (Exodus 3:12), which means receiving the Torah, and they were occupied with the spoil of the sea and did not say, 'Let us go and run to receive the Torah'; therefore they were punished with a lack of water, as at Rephidim, where because they slackened their hands from the Torah, therefore it is also said there, ״וַיַּחֲנוּ בִּרְפִידִים וְאֵין מַיִם לִשְׁתֹּת הָעָם״ (Exodus 17:1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "The Talmudic passage is cited in Bava Kamma 82b; the text reads 'בבא קמא (פב)' using a peh-beit page abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:46.300842386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}